{
 "manufacturer": "Elkor",
 "manufacturer_slug": "elkor",
 "model": "WattsOn-Mark II -E4 power meter (BACnet IP)",
 "model_slug": "wattson-mark-ii-e4-bacnet-ip",
 "aliases": [
  "WattsOn-Mark II",
  "WattsOn Mk II",
  "W2-E4",
  "WattsOn-MkII-E4",
  "Elkor WattsOn BACnet IP"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter (submeter)",
 "applies_to": "Elkor WattsOn-Mark II power meters with the -E4 Ethernet/Wi-Fi option, which adds BACnet IP.",
 "summary": "The -E4 version of the WattsOn-Mark II serves its metering data over BACnet IP from an Ethernet or Wi-Fi module. Metering objects use the Modbus register offset as the instance: totals and per-phase power, voltage, current, power factor and angles, plus energy registers by quadrant. Writable Analog Values set CT/PT ratios, demand window, relay alarms and energy reset; the 70000/80000 ranges show network status and settings.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Metering, configuration and relay objects use the Modbus register offset as the instance number (0-65535); network status is at 70000-79999 and network settings at 80000-89999.",
  "The unit text for kVAR and kVA is swapped in the table (kVAR objects say kilovolt-amperes, kVA objects say kilovolt-amperes-reactive), and kVAh_Import/Export_A-C say kilowatt-hours; units here follow the printed BACnet unit codes (12 = kvar, 9 = kVA, 240 = kVAh).",
  "The 6 Structured View objects (SV 0-5) are not listed here. The network status rows are typed 'CS' in the table and are listed as CharacterString Values.",
  "Input_Config (CT type: 1 mA, 2 mV, 3 5 A, 4 Rogowski, 0 custom) is printed with no instance number and is left out.",
  "Network settings (80000 range) are read-only over BACnet and are changed in the web interface.",
  "MSI 70000, CSV 70000 and DTV 70000 share the instance number but are different object types."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "WattsOn-Mark II BACnet/IP (-E4) BACnet Object List",
  "doc_number": null,
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.elkor.net/pdfs/WattsOn-MkII-BACnet-E4_Object_List.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Set the CT and PT ratios (AV 1280-1295) to match the installation, then read total kW, kWh import, demand, power factor, average current and voltage. Energy totals are zeroed by writing 42405 to Reset_Energy.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "AI 512",
    "name": "kW_Total",
    "why": "Total real power, kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 4356",
    "name": "kWh_Import_Ttl",
    "why": "Imported energy total, kWh"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 4352",
    "name": "kWh_Net_Ttl",
    "why": "Net energy total, kWh"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 598",
    "name": "kW_Demand",
    "why": "Sliding-window kW demand"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 524",
    "name": "PF_Total",
    "why": "Total power factor"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 522",
    "name": "Current_Avg",
    "why": "Average current, A"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 518",
    "name": "Volts_LN_Avg",
    "why": "Average line-to-neutral voltage, V"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 526",
    "name": "Frequency",
    "why": "Line frequency, Hz"
   }
  ],
  "enable": null,
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet port, device instance (-1 = derived from the MAC), APDU size, segmentation and BBMD foreign registration are set in the web interface; objects 80070-80078 (CSV and BI) show the values.",
   "Ethernet or Wi-Fi can be static or DHCP; the active link and IP show at MI 70000 and CSV 70000-70006.",
   "Set CT_Primary/Secondary_All and PT_Primary/Secondary_All (or the per-phase AVs) before trusting readings."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Reset_Energy only acts on the value 42405 (0xA5A5); Reboot_Device only on 43605 (0xAA55).",
   "With the meter locked (BV 1321), settings writes need the passcode entered at PIV 1319.",
   "kVAR/kVA unit text in the source table is swapped; trust the unit codes."
  ]
 },
